WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.048
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambridge exams.

2
00:00:05.348 --> 00:00:08.851
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.151 --> 00:00:18.165
Unit eighteen: C1 Advanced: Writing Essays, Proposals and Reports. Today you will write a persuasive essay and a formal proposal or report.

4
00:00:18.465 --> 00:00:21.269
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:22.233 --> 00:00:25.466
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:26.317 --> 00:00:27.504
Persuasive.

7
00:00:28.517 --> 00:00:30.934
Persuasive means able to convince people.

8
00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:33.294
Write a persuasive essay.

9
00:00:33.883 --> 00:00:36.489
Your turn. Say: Persuasive.

10
00:00:39.333 --> 00:00:40.613
Persuasive.

11
00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:42.351
Proposal.

12
00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:46.499
Proposal means a formal plan with recommendations.

13
00:00:47.083 --> 00:00:49.176
Write a proposal for the council.

14
00:00:49.783 --> 00:00:52.412
Your turn. Say: Proposal.

15
00:00:55.267 --> 00:00:56.221
Proposal.

16
00:00:56.983 --> 00:00:57.961
Recommend.

17
00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:01.321
Recommend means to suggest as the best.

18
00:01:01.917 --> 00:01:03.905
I recommend a new library.

19
00:01:04.517 --> 00:01:07.401
Your turn. Say: Recommend.

20
00:01:10.267 --> 00:01:11.407
Recommend.

21
00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:13.232
Evaluate.

22
00:01:14.217 --> 00:01:16.994
Evaluate means to judge the value of something.

23
00:01:17.583 --> 00:01:19.467
Evaluate both options.

24
00:01:20.083 --> 00:01:23.049
Your turn. Say: Evaluate.

25
00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:27.110
Evaluate.

26
00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:28.793
Cohesion.

27
00:01:29.783 --> 00:01:32.398
Cohesion means the connection between ideas.

28
00:01:32.983 --> 00:01:34.379
Check cohesion.

29
00:01:34.983 --> 00:01:37.403
Your turn. Say: Cohesion.

30
00:01:40.267 --> 00:01:41.361
Cohesion.

31
00:01:42.117 --> 00:01:43.060
Nuanced.

32
00:01:44.050 --> 00:01:47.106
Nuanced means showing small differences in meaning.

33
00:01:47.717 --> 00:01:49.147
A nuanced argument.

34
00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:52.135
Your turn. Say: Nuanced.

35
00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:55.850
Nuanced.

36
00:01:56.617 --> 00:01:57.571
Concede.

37
00:01:58.583 --> 00:02:01.790
Concede means to accept that part of an opposing view is true.

38
00:02:02.383 --> 00:02:04.511
I concede that costs matter.

39
00:02:05.117 --> 00:02:07.630
Your turn. Say: Concede.

40
00:02:10.467 --> 00:02:11.328
Concede.

41
00:02:12.083 --> 00:02:13.154
Formal tone.

42
00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:16.788
Formal tone means a serious and polite style.

43
00:02:17.383 --> 00:02:18.849
Use a formal tone.

44
00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:22.033
Your turn. Say: Formal tone.

45
00:02:24.867 --> 00:02:26.112
Formal tone.

46
00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:30.435
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:31.283 --> 00:02:33.689
Visal, what makes C1 Writing different?

48
00:02:34.783 --> 00:02:47.037
The essay is compulsory and asks you to evaluate two ideas and say which is more important. The second task offers a proposal, report, letter or review.

49
00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:49.952
How do I write a strong essay?

50
00:02:51.050 --> 00:03:04.233
Use a clear thesis, develop each idea with examples and concede a counterpoint. Use a range of structures and vocabulary precisely, and keep the argument cohesive.

51
00:03:05.317 --> 00:03:06.945
How do I write a proposal?

52
00:03:08.050 --> 00:03:18.853
Use headings, a formal tone and clear recommendations. Describe the situation, evaluate the options and finish with a persuasive conclusion.

53
00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:21.698
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:27.649
Grammar focus: Strategy: thesis, evaluation, recommendation.

55
00:03:27.949 --> 00:03:29.218
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:29.917 --> 00:03:33.391
While cost is important, safety should be the first priority.

57
00:03:34.283 --> 00:03:37.653
I strongly recommend that the council build a new library.

58
00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:47.173
Plan a clear thesis, evaluate both sides with precise language and use a formal tone. In a proposal, finish with a persuasive recommendation.

59
00:03:47.917 --> 00:03:51.916
Be careful! Don't say: I write an essay without a thesis.

60
00:03:53.867 --> 00:03:55.971
Say: I state a clear thesis.

61
00:03:56.271 --> 00:03:57.330
Thesis first.

62
00:03:58.133 --> 00:04:01.018
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:04:01.833 --> 00:04:03.194
A Formal Proposal.

64
00:04:03.494 --> 00:04:06.864
The council asks for a proposal to improve the town centre.

65
00:04:07.867 --> 00:04:10.423
Lakhena divides her proposal with headings.

66
00:04:11.433 --> 00:04:14.791
She evaluates two options and concedes that one is cheaper.

67
00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:19.460
She recommends the second option because it benefits more people.

68
00:04:20.467 --> 00:04:23.082
She uses a formal tone and checks cohesion.

69
00:04:24.167 --> 00:04:27.867
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:28.717 --> 00:04:30.484
The C1 essay is blank.

71
00:04:30.784 --> 00:04:34.658
A, compulsory. B, optional. C, oral.

72
00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:40.641
The answer is A: compulsory.

73
00:04:41.783 --> 00:04:43.504
A proposal uses blank.

74
00:04:43.804 --> 00:04:48.700
A, no structure. B, headings and recommendations. C, emojis.

75
00:04:52.233 --> 00:04:55.255
The answer is B: headings and recommendations.

76
00:04:56.417 --> 00:04:58.068
To concede means to blank.

77
00:04:58.368 --> 00:05:02.822
A, refuse. B, stop writing. C, accept part of the other view.

78
00:05:06.367 --> 00:05:09.945
The answer is C: accept part of the other view.

79
00:05:11.083 --> 00:05:12.851
What does Lakhena recommend?

80
00:05:13.151 --> 00:05:17.721
A, the second option. B, doing nothing. C, the cheaper only.

81
00:05:21.267 --> 00:05:23.719
The answer is A: the second option.

82
00:05:24.883 --> 00:05:26.477
The tone should be blank.

83
00:05:26.777 --> 00:05:29.908
A, angry. B, formal. C, slangy.

84
00:05:33.467 --> 00:05:35.246
The answer is B: formal.

85
00:05:36.433 --> 00:05:39.840
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:40.683 --> 00:05:42.880
How do you write a persuasive proposal?

87
00:05:51.683 --> 00:05:53.230
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:53.530 --> 00:06:09.560
I plan the headings and decide my recommendation first. I describe the situation, evaluate the options and concede a point from the other side to show balance. I finish with a clear recommendation, using a formal tone.

89
00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:11.674
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:06:12.583 --> 00:06:19.067
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: thesis, evaluation, recommendation.

91
00:06:19.367 --> 00:06:24.365
Today's value is practical wisdom. Judge ideas by how well they work in real life.

92
00:06:24.665 --> 00:06:27.317
See you in Unit nineteen. Goodbye!

93
00:06:27.617 --> 00:06:30.223
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

